273 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Even after the amendment, DRC-01A remains the only prescribed statutory mechanism through which the department can \(i\) communicate the proposed tax liability, \(ii\) enable voluntary payment, and \(iii\) avoid unnecessary litigation. Therefore, treating Rule 142\(1A\) as purely discretionary is inconsistent with the structure of Sections 73 and 74.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
274 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The Andhra Pradesh High Court has repeatedly taken this view. In Satyanarayana Medical Distributors \(Writ Petition No. 35710 of 2022, decided on 12.02. 2025\), it categorically held that omission to issue DRC-01A is a violation of natural justice and vitiates the entire adjudication. The present judgment continues this judicial line, recognising that pre-notice consultation is not an empty formality but a procedural right intended to prevent premature escalation to litigation and ensure proportionality in tax administration.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
