377 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This ruling reinforces the statutory design that recovery under Section 79\(1\)\(a\) can validly commence once the three-month period for payment under Section 78 expires, unless a stay is obtained. While the Act allows an additional condonable period for appeal, that extension is not a matter of right and does not defer recovery unless the appellate forum grants protection. Thus, mere availability of an extended appeal window does not prevent the department from invoking Section 79 upon expiry of the initial three months.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
